        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are basement water alarms worth it?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Few things in a basement have a better ratio of cost to avoided damage. A point alarm is ten to twenty dollars against a category of damage that regularly runs to five figures, and water damage is consistently among the most common homeowners insurance claims. It works by collapsing discovery time, which is what actually determines the cost."
